  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "cma-159144-0",
      "field": "inscriptions[0].inscription_translation",
      "text": "On the day of wu, the first month, the first year of Yongkang, I made the bright mirror at the first of dawn by refining the yellow and the white [metals].  Great fortune and wealth will come as a result.  May you live a long life. Up above are the King Father [of the East] and the Queen Mother of \nthe West.",
      "source_text": "永康元年正月午日，由（幽）【涑】黃日（白）。\n早作明鏡，大吉大宮（富）。\n延長壽命，上有王父西王母。",
      "remark": ""
    }
  ],
